 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? It depends on how much you ride and what kind of riding you do. Roughly speaking, tire life is usually one or two months of Sunday riding. Most tires give good warning before they blow. A sudden increase in resistance as the tire hits the valve is the biggest clue. That doesn't hurt much as long as you keep the tube between the tire and any sharps. Generally yes, lower pressure when it' wet, because the tire doesn't lose pressure slowly, it starts to feel like it's going to blow right away.",
